#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""paranoid-lake-update: see what `lake update` would pull in before you run it.

`lake update` clones every new dependency revision and then *executes* each
dependency's `lakefile.lean` to configure it.  A malicious commit upstream
therefore runs on your machine (or in CI, holding tokens) before you have any
chance to look at it.  This tool predicts the update using nothing but `git`
(bare clones, no checkout, no hooks, no Lake), writes the full diff of every
dependency that would change, flags files and patterns worth a close look, and
optionally hands the result to an AI auditor and/or publishes it.

Commands (see `--help` on each):

  plan      Predict what a bare `lake update` would do in this package.
  compare   Diff the dependency changes between two manifests / git refs
            (for example base branch vs an update PR).
  range     Diff one repository between two revisions.
  watch     Audit new commits on a branch since the last run (state file).
  audit     Run an AI auditor on an existing output directory.
  publish   Upload an output directory as a gist and/or comment on a PR.
  prompt    Print the audit prompt for an output directory.

Only the Python standard library, `git`, and (for publishing) `gh` are used.
"""

